mlx_metal_wide_reserve (mlx-serve, off until a caller arms it): a reserve of large Metal buffers outside MLX's cache.
The caller arms it with a byte floor and a list of sizes; the buffers are allocated and written once at the call (their
pages mapped then). An allocation of at least the floor that MLX's cache cannot serve takes the smallest idle reserve
buffer at least its size (the cache only serves within two pages of the size); its free puts it back. clear_cache and
the cache limit never release the reserve; disarming (floor 0) releases its idle buffers. Its bytes count as MLX's
active memory from the arming on, idle or in use, so a budget read from MLX's counters sees them.
mlx_metal_wide_reserve_stats reads its floor, size and hit counts; mlx_metal_wide_reserve_plant is the tests' planted
aliasing bug (every hit shares one buffer). MLX_METAL_WIDE_LOG (diagnostic) prints each armed miss. Unarmed, MLX's own
paths are unchanged (one load and test per allocation and free).

Used by mlx-serve's DeepSeek-V4.1 plugin (MLX_SERVE_DSV41_PF_KEEP_WIDE): a prompt pass's large intermediates, freshly
allocated by every request's first layer (the engine clears MLX's cache at each request's end), come from the reserve.
Not reported upstream.

